00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.040
- This is a special place, for sure.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.200
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.480
On the 14th of February, 1990,

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:53.200
the Voyager 1 spacecraft was
about 6 billion kilometers

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.040
from the sun when it took this picture.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.880
All you see are a few rays
of light and a little dot.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:05.320
Carl Sagan described this picture best.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.240
(gentle music)
"Look again at that dot.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.640
That's here, that's home, that's us.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:13.960
On it, everyone you
love, everyone you know.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.800
Everyone you ever heard of,

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.720
every human being who ever
was lived out their lives,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.800
every hero and coward,

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.080
every creator and
destroyer of civilization,

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.600
every young couple in love,

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.280
every mother and father,
inventor and explorer,

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.680
every superstar, every supreme leader,

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.040
every saint and sinner

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.000
in the history of our species lived there,

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.200
on a mote of dust suspended in a sunbeam."

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:47.200
The earth is a very small
stage in a vast cosmic arena.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.240
To me, it underscores our responsibility

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.840
to deal more kindly with one another,

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.680
and to preserve and
cherish the pale blue dot,

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:59.920
the only home we've ever known.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.280
- I'm glad you taught me something today.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.560
